                        "recommendationid": "238917233",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198059825119",
                            "num_reviews": 300,
                            "playtime_forever": 1316,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 872,
                            "playtime_at_review": 1316,
                            "last_played": 1793314315
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Trine 2 is a solid puzzle platformer, visually stunning and with very nice music tracks. The story and combat are basic. You use your 3 characters with their unique skills to solve the myriad of puzzles and to defeat opponents. There are also some easy also boss battles, which is a nice refreshment from the incredibly frustrating boss battles I encountered in some other similar games. The puzzles are also moderate in difficulty, you can solve more or less all of them with a little pondering and using logic. That is also a good refreshment. \r\nThe game comes with the free DLC: Goblin Menace, which is much harder then the base game but still doable. However, for the DLC I had to use the playthrough from time to time because some puzzles were hard. If someone asked me to detect a shortcoming, it would be that Trine 2 is too much focused on finding the experience bubbles ( little blue bubbles all around the map ). Some times it can be frustrating to collect them all, but it's not required to have them all. They are used to unlock skills but you don't need all the skills, and by the time you reach the end-game you will have all the skills you need. \r\nA very pleasant fantasy experience.",
